      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should include scope_types, too (unfortunately). If an operator doesn\u0027t set enforce_scope \u003d True, then anyone with the reader role (on a project, domain, or system) will be able to list role assignments, which would be a regression.\n\nFor example:\n\n  (role:reader and system_scope:all)\n\nWould make sure we implement system reader\n\n  (role:reader and domain_id:%(target.domain_id)s)\n\nWould implement domain reader if we make sure we populate the domain id in the target when we process the request. I had to take a similar approach when implementing support for that here [0][1]\n\n[0] https://review.openstack.org/#/c/623319/5/keystone/common/policies/user.py\n[1] https://review.openstack.org/#/c/623319/5/keystone/api/users.py@167",
